  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "OpenccNetLib v1.6.2\n\n            - Added a net9.0 target asset for modern runtime optimizations while retaining netstandard2.0 as the primary compatibility target and fallback.\n            - Optimized conversion, compatibility normalization, text splitting, IDS preservation, and DeTofu on .NET 9+ to reduce allocations and improve throughput while preserving the established netstandard2.0 paths.\n            - Added Opencc.NormalizeUnicodeCompat() for curated scalar-preserving CJK Unicode compatibility, punctuation, and text-extraction normalization.\n            - Extended Opencc.NormalizeCompat() with optional extended Unicode compatibility normalization while preserving its default behavior.\n            - Added canonical custom-dictionary token parsing with strict DictSlot validation and portable <slot>:<append|override>:<path> syntax.\n            - Added an optional punctuation argument to direct Traditional → Traditional regional conversion APIs.\n            - Improved DeTofu with Unicode scalar lookup, cached built-in mapping data, and independently mutable built-in maps.\n            - Updated conversion dictionaries and curated Unicode compatibility mappings.\n            - Expanded differential, randomized, Unicode, IDS, DeTofu, and malformed-input test coverage.\n            - Refactored Office/EPUB package processing into two entry-by-entry paths: pure in-memory ConvertOfficeBytes() APIs and separate streaming ConvertOfficeFile() APIs with validated temporary-file publication, while preserving EPUB packaging requirements.\n\n            Breaking: custom dictionary bundles must include jps_characters_rev; regenerate custom JSON/CBOR/Zstd bundles for v1.6.x.",
